PS1's lineage is in timeline/lineage.md, from the record at both ends.

What the day reused, in the order it arrived, each with its commit: the sgit.ai sites' way of working (1f7c633, 00:40); CLAUDE.md "modelled on web-summit.sgit.ai" (97b98d9); the editor's key tool from pki.sgit.ai, its hash matching the PHP newsroom's pinned copy (17b287b); the PHP newsroom's session banners (a3a4807); SGit's vaults (defe526); Issues-FS and Email-FS "in web-summit.sgit.ai's pattern" (31b0f86); ruv.sgit.ai's player and studio pieces (3314ffe, c3ce566); Wardley maps (df37797).

What the day invented: the schedule, the hold, the five-step wake, the locks, the follow-ups. The plumbing came from earlier projects; the controls were made that night.

What it handed on: this book's team ported the talk's rules, wake protocol and key tool, as its own files say, and took its book roles from the Gen ZX Founders book; then improved the factory (sessions handed between accounts with new keys; slower cadences when idle). One project's controls became the next one's starting point.

